{"name":"Green Beret","hex":"#516a62","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Green Beret","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the United States Army Special Forces."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Green_Beret"}],"entries":[{"title":"Commandos (United Kingdom)","blocks":[{"text":"The Commandos, also known as the British Commandos, were formed during the Second World War in June 1940, following a request from Winston Churchill, for special forces that could carry out raids against German-occupied Europe. Initially drawn from within the British Army from soldiers who volunteered for the Special Service Brigade, the Commandos' ranks were eventually filled by members of all branches of the British Armed Forces and a number of foreign volunteers from German-occupied countries. By the end of the war 25,000 men had passed through the Commando course at Achnacarry. This total includes not only the British volunteers, but volunteers from Greece, France, Belgium, Netherlands, Canada, Norway and Poland. The United States Army Rangers and US Marine Corps Raiders were modelled on the Commandos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/The_Commando_Memorial_%287%29.jpg/330px-The_Commando_Memorial_%287%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commandos_(United_Kingdom)","wikidata":"Q2347548"},{"title":"United States Army Special Forces","blocks":[{"text":"The United States Army Special Forces (SF), colloquially known as the \"Green Berets\" due to their distinctive service headgear, is a branch of the United States Army Special Operations Command (USASOC)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/USA_-_Special_Forces_Branch_Insignia.png/330px-USA_-_Special_Forces_Branch_Insignia.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Army_Special_Forces","wikidata":"Q482421"},{"title":"Green beret","blocks":[{"text":"The green beret is a form of headdress in use by a number of militaries worldwide, primarily by those with commando and or special operations backgrounds. It was the official headgear of the British Commandos, a special-forces unit active during World War II and is still worn by members of the Royal Marines after passing the Commando Course, and personnel from other units of the Royal Navy, Army and RAF who serve within UK Commando Force and who have passed the All Arms Commando Course. Green berets are similarly the official beret color of the United States Army Special Forces, and source of their autonymous moniker \"The Green Berets\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Evening_Parade_140718-M-GR671-137.jpg/330px-Evening_Parade_140718-M-GR671-137.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_beret","wikidata":"Q11680250"},{"title":"Beret","blocks":[{"text":"A beret is a soft, round, flat-crowned cap made of hand-knitted wool, crocheted cotton, wool felt, or acrylic fibre."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Sven_Palmqvist_1965.jpg/330px-Sven_Palmqvist_1965.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beret","wikidata":"Q211718"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/British_Generals_1939-1945_H39029.jpg/500px-British_Generals_1939-1945_H39029.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/British_Generals_1939-1945_H39029.jpg/1280px-British_Generals_1939-1945_H39029.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/British_Generals_1939-1945_H39029.jpg/500px-Brit